Brain protein abundance data previously obtained by mass spectrometry from DLPFC in ROSMAP9 were paired with plasma SomaScan protein measurements in ROSMAP to assess plasma–brain associations. Analysis was restricted to 216 white individuals with plasma measurements within 3 years of autopsy. Matching between plasma and brain protein was performed at the gene symbol level. For the subset of 4,171 plasma–brain protein pairs with matching gene symbols, a linear model was used to assess the predictive relationship between plasma protein abundance and brain protein abundance while controlling for time to death and demographic covariates. Specifically, for each pair, the following model was applied:6\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
