				\begin{document}$$n$$\end{document}n denotes the number of samples, for all assays of a sample, and then unlogging all data. The protein assays most statistically significantly associated with cerebral β-amyloidosis from the meta-analysis in both positive and negative directions were divided into 42 candidate numerator and 42 denominator groups, respectively. For the non-APOE ε4 analysis, 46 numerator and 46 denominator candidates from the APOE ε4-independent protein list were tested. For the cohort-specific analysis, 30 numerator and 30 denominator candidates from each cohort-specific linear model analysis results were tested. Unweighted (equal assay weight) ratios of the unlogged assay summed numerator and denominator data were computed for all possible protein combinations within and across numerators and denominators, starting with single-gene ratios (1:1) and extending to higher-order combinations (for example, 2:2, 3:3 and 4:4). Each ratio was rated for biweight midcorrelation (bicor) to the linear measure of amyloid positivity available for that cohort and for the receiver operating characteristic (ROC) AUC value for prediction of the binary trait of amyloid positivity. After computation, results were aggregated and ranked based on bicor and AUC values, with the top AUC-ranked ratios retained and identified as potential synthetic biomarkers. The top-performing ratios’ predictive performance across different ratio combinations (for example, 1:1, 2:2, 3:3 and 4:4) were visualized individually and in combination with the covariates age, sex and APOE status.

Cox proportional hazard regression models were used to calculate risk of cognitive impairment in ROSMAP using the ‘survival’ package (version 3.5-3) in R. Time to conversion from normal cognitive function to impaired cognitive function was calculated in months. If there was no conversion noted at any annual visit from the clinical cognitive diagnosis summary score (1 = no impairment), a binary event status of 0 was assigned to the participant. If there was an increment in the summary score (greater than 1), a binary event status of 1 was assigned to the participant. A change in cognitive status did not have to occur within 3 years of autopsy. Three separate analyses were performed to assess proteins associated with risk of incident impairment: (1) all participants (n = 310 total with n = 172 converters); (2) participants restricted to those with confirmed AD pathology at autopsy as previously described9 (n = 269 total with n = 131 converters); and (3) same as in (2) but with non-converters restricted to participants with minimal to no AD pathology at autopsy as previously described9 (n = 187 total with n = 131 converters). Participants with frontotemporal dementia or vascular dementia diagnoses were excluded from all analyses. All log2(abundance) protein measures were standardized using z-transformation before inclusion in the model. Key demographic and clinical covariates were included in the model, namely age, sex, years of education, the global cognition score and APOE ε4 carrier status:7\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
