A five-fold cross-validation scheme was also employed to test robustness and generalizability of the models. In each fold, the dataset was partitioned into training (80%) and validation (20%) subsets. Feature importance was analyzed based on stability across cross-validation iterations. Hazard ratios (HR), 95% confidence intervals (CI) and associated two-tailed P values were determined for each protein. A two-tailed P < 0.05 was calculated as:\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
