				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$$2{\times} \left(1-\Phi \left(\left|\frac{\mathrm{ln}\left({\rm{HR}}\right)-\mathrm{ln}(1)}{\left(\frac{95 \% {\rm{CIupper}}-95 \% {\rm{CIlower}}}{2{\times} 1.96}\right)}\right|\right)\right)$$\end{document}2×1−ΦlnHR−ln(1)95%CIupper−95%CIlower2×1.96where Φ represents the cumulative density function of the standard normal distribution. The concordance index (C-index) was computed to evaluate model discrimination, and the log-rank test was performed to compare survival distributions.
